/-!
# Composition of bounds across scales, continued: the tree-gauge bridge, aligned covers and a
# mixing interface

A Lean 4 / Mathlib development about multiscale bounds. It continues the series from Parts 1–9, and
its parts are numbered 10–12. It does not import Parts 1–9: where a part uses one of their
definitions or statements, it re-defines or re-proves it. Each part was written as a separate module
and is wrapped here in its own `section`, so that its `open` commands stay local; the namespaces are
distinct, so no names clash.

| part | section | namespace | content |
|---|---|---|---|
| 10 | `Part10_TreeGaugeBridge` | `TreeGaugeBridge` | the tree-gauge bridge for the one-shot loss at Gaussian order: minimisers on an affine set and the curvature transfer; the weighted curvature energy (the commutator step); the curvature mass and the constant `κ_lead`; shell sums; the tree-gauge `ℓ¹` constant and the level sum; the composed loss bound; examples and witnesses |
| 11 | `Part11_AlignedCoverPoincare` | `AlignedCoverPoincare` | an aligned-cover Poincaré inequality in two dimensions, uniform in depth: the constant chain of the two-level decomposition; one-dimensional dual-norm and tent arithmetic; the Lions-type step and its converse; transport through the curvature isometry; first-chaos variance tensorisation; surjectivity, ergodicity and codimension across depths; the exact depth-0 value; examples and witnesses |
| 12 | `Part12_InterfaceMIX` | `InterfaceMIX` | a mixing interface: covariance algebra and the law of total covariance (A1); symmetric positive operators (eigen-mass bound, decay and eigenvalue bounds, norm gap versus eigenvalue gap); Lemma IR (transfer-operator gap and `L²` mixing, with the converse in finite dimensions); clustering and the spectral gap; Theorem MIX (UV, localisation and IR bounds give exponential decay of covariances); examples and witnesses |

## Main results

* **Minimisers and the curvature transfer** (Part 10). Two minimisers of a positive semidefinite
  symmetric bilinear form `B` on an affine set `Σ₀ ∩ {A x = y}` have the same value and differ by
  an element of `Σ₀ ∩ ker A ∩ ker B`; for `Q = ‖F·‖²` they have the same image, `F u = F u'`
  (`sub_mem_ker_of_minimizers`, `map_eq_of_minimizers`, `mulVec_eq_of_minimizers`). Minimality
  passes from a section under gauge fixing, and from a penalised problem whose penalty `R ≥ 0`
  vanishes at a minimiser (`minimizer_of_section`, `minimizer_of_penalty`). Hence a tree column
  `T`, minimal on the tree section, and a smooth column `u`, minimal for `Q + R`, have the same
  curvature `D T = D u`, provided gauge fixing does not raise `Q` and some admissible `v` has
  `R(v) = 0` and `Q(v) ≤ Q(T)` (`curvature_transfer`).
* **Weighted curvature energy** (Part 10). If the rows of `|D|` sum to at most `4`, its columns to
  at most `6`, and the weights are `λ₀/2^k`-Lipschitz along the incidence, then the energy-norm
  bound `Q(e^f u) + 4^{−k}‖e^f u‖² ≤ (2𝔐)²` gives `Σ_p e^{2g(p)} (D u)_p² ≤ 8𝔐²` for `λ₀ ≥ 0`
  with `96 λ₀² ≤ 1`, and `Σ_p e^{2g(p)} (D u)_p² ≤ 4𝔐²(1 + 96 λ₀²)` for `0 < λ₀ ≤ 1`
  (`add_sq_le_young`, `commutator_energy_le_young`, `commutator_energy_le`,
  `weighted_curvature_le`, `weighted_curvature_le_young`).
* **Curvature mass and the constant `κ_lead`** (Part 10). Let `κ_lead = 24√2 𝔐/λ₀²`
  (`kappaLead`), `𝔐, q ≥ 0`, and `Σ_p e^{−2g(p)} ≤ 144 (2^k/λ₀)⁴ q`. Then `‖x‖₁/4^k ≤ √q κ_lead`
  if `Σ_p e^{2g(p)} x_p² ≤ 8𝔐²`, and `‖x‖₁/4^k ≤ κ_lead` if
  `Σ_p e^{2g(p)} x_p² ≤ 4𝔐²(1 + 96 λ₀²)` and `q (1 + 96 λ₀²) ≤ 2` (`l1_sq_le`,
  `curvature_mass_le_of_sq`, `curvature_mass_le`, `curvature_mass_le_lead`). Moreover
  `√q κ_lead ≤ 34 𝔐/λ₀²` for `0 ≤ q ≤ 289/288` (`sqrt_mul_kappaLead_le`, `kappaLead_le`), and
  `κ_lead ≤ 1.4·10⁵⁴` for `0 ≤ 𝔐 ≤ 6.34·10¹¹` and `λ₀ ≥ 3.928·10⁻²¹` (`kappaLead_numeric_le`).
* **Shell sums** (Part 10). `Σ_{r<R} (64 r³ + 16 r + 1) x^r ≤ 384/(1 − x)⁴` for `0 ≤ x < 1`, and
  `Σ_{r<R} (64 r³ + 16 r + 1) e^{−br} ≤ 384 e^{4b}/b⁴` for `b > 0`; at `b = 2λ₀/2^k`, `λ₀ > 0`,
  six times the right side is `144 (2^k/λ₀)⁴ e^{4b}` (`choose_three_cast`, `shell_series_le`,
  `mul_exp_neg_le_one_sub`, `shell_weight_le`, `weight_bound_eq`). For `0 ≤ b ≤ 2·10⁻⁴` and
  `𝔐 ≥ 0`, `e^{2b} κ_lead ≤ 34 𝔐/λ₀²` (`exp_sq_mul_kappaLead_le`).
* **The tree-gauge `ℓ¹` constant** (Part 10). The local constants `c₁ = 1` and `c₂ ≤ 7/2`
  (`internal_link_le`, `crossing_link_le`); the constant `C_d = 2d · 2^{d−1} c₂ + c₁ c_B`
  (`treeConst`), with `C₄ = 64 c₂ + c₁ c_B` (`treeConst_four`), `C₄ ≤ 241` for `c₁ = 1`,
  `c_B = 17` and `c₂ ≤ 7/2` (`treeConst_four_le`; the count `4 · 2³ − 15 = 17` is
  `block_link_count`), and `C₄ ≤ 128` under the stronger inputs `c₂ ≤ 31/16` and `c₁ c_B ≤ 4`,
  which are hypotheses (`treeConst_four_le_128`). For `d ≥ 2` the level sum costs no logarithm: a
  telescoped estimate with these coefficients and the contraction `F_i ≤ 2^{−(d−2)i} F₀` gives
  `Φ ≤ s a + C_d (2^k − 1) F₀` (`level_sum_bound`, `tree_l1_le`).
* **The one-shot loss in the tree gauge** (Part 10). For a field `φ` with `‖Aφ‖₁ = 1`, the
  curvature of `u`, and the tree-gauge `ℓ¹` inequality `‖φ‖₁ ≤ 8^k ‖Aφ‖₁ + C 2^k ‖Dφ‖₁` with
  `C ≥ 0`, under the hypotheses of the previous items: `‖φ‖₁/8^k ≤ 1 + C √q κ_lead`, and
  `‖φ‖₁/8^k ≤ 1 + C κ_lead` when `q (1 + 96 λ₀²) ≤ 2` (`loss_le`, `oneShot_loss_le`,
  `oneShot_loss_le_lead`). With the curvature transfer, the shell-count hypothesis,
  `0 < λ₀ ≤ 10⁻⁴` and `0 ≤ C ≤ 241`, the tree column satisfies `D T = D u`,
  `‖D T‖₁/4^k ≤ √(e^{8λ₀/2^k}) κ_lead`, `‖D T‖₁/4^k ≤ κ_lead`, `‖T‖₁/8^k ≤ 1 + 241 κ_lead` and
  `‖T‖₁/8^k ≤ 1 + 241 · 34 𝔐/λ₀²` (`tree_gauge_loss_le`); the last right side is at most
  `3.4·10⁵⁶` for `𝔐 ≤ 6.34·10¹¹` and `λ₀ ≥ 3.928·10⁻²¹` (`loss_numeric`).
* **The constant chain of the two-level decomposition** (Part 11). `C₀(C) = 2 + 2048 (C + 9/16)`
  (`twoLevelConst`) equals `14986/5 = 2997.2` at `C = 9/10`, and `1/(9 C₀) = 5/134874 ≥ 1/26975`
